course: dictionary
lesson: 2316
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word cross is a good example. Read the words around it to find its meaning, just as you would with any new word.
explain: «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone.» Here crossed means went from one side to the other. The clue is the street: you cannot cross a street and stay on the same side of it.
explain: «Mum was cross when we came home late.» Here cross means angry. Mum is not walking anywhere or drawing a mark, so the meaning must be about feelings. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Cross can be a verb, a noun or an adjective.
fact: To cross means to go from one side to the other, like across a road, river or bridge.
fact: A cross is a mark like × or +. The multiplication sign × looks like a cross.
fact: To cross out means to draw a line through a word or number.
fact: Cross as an adjective means angry, and it is often used to describe a person's mood.
exercise: «A boy in California crossed a street while looking at his phone.» What does crossed mean here? | Put his arms over each other | Drew a line through the street | *Went from one side to the other | Got angry at the street
exercise: In maths, you are asked to cross out the even numbers. What does cross out mean? | To go over a bridge | *To draw a line through | To write a plus sign | To be angry with the numbers
exercise: «Mum was cross when we came home late.» What does cross mean? | *Angry | To put one leg over the other | To go across a bridge | A mark like ×
test: In the sum 3 × 4, the × sign looks like a what? | *A cross | A street | A chokepoint | A flask
test: «A flask has two walls, so heat can hardly cross.» What does cross mean here? | Hold your fingers together | *Go from one side to the other | Draw a line through | Get angry
exam: «Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes on giant ships.» What does cross mean in this sentence? | To be angry with the sea | *To go from one side of the sea to the other | To draw a line through the sea | To cover the sea with a lid
